  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Fall pattern continues with multiple chances \nfor showers through the weekend; however, no hazardous weather \nis expected.\n\nCurrent radar outlines some shower activity across the Poconos \nand into portions of eastern New York and will likely continue \nto bring some rain chances over the next couple of hours to the \neastern half of the forecast area. Recent surface analysis does \noutline a cold front across a SYR-UNV-MRB line could bring some \nadditional shower activity over the next couple of hours further\nwest which is outlines fairly well in REFS guidance. Given this\npotential, have added some shower chances across this region; \nhowever, accumulations will generally be light and be nothing \nmore than some light, beneficial rainfall across the region.\n\nAs this cold front shifts east of the region tonight, drier air\nbegins to work into the forecast area, with mainly dry \nconditions on tap for Friday. The area of low pressure stationed\nacross the Mid-Atlantic Coast and across the Great Lakes could \nbring some light showers late Friday, but best chances appear to\nbe west/east of the area at this time. Shower potential \nincreases more markedly for the weekend, with an area of low \npressure moving across southwestern Ontario and into New York \nState. All model guidance continues to point towards rainfall \nbeing light with this system with periods of rain through Sunday\nmorning before another shortwave trough dips down across the \nregion and brings additional rain chances late Sunday and into \nMonday. A slight reprieve from dry conditions appear possible \nlate Monday through Wednesday based on LREF ensemble guidance, \nbefore an unsettled pattern takes hold of the region for later \nin the week.",
